# Sprint 16 — pfSense Firewall & Network Segmentation

## Objective

Deploy pfSense into the SOC home lab to introduce network segmentation between the existing corporate lab environment and a dedicated attacker network.

This sprint establishes **KALI01** as a segmented attack workstation behind **FW01**, allowing future attack simulations to traverse a firewall rather than originating directly from the corporate network.

---

## Lab Architecture

### FW01 — pfSense CE 2.8.1

| Interface | NIC | Network | IP Address | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| WAN | em0 | VMware NAT | DHCP | External connectivity |
| LAN | em1 | LAB_NET | 10.10.10.1/24 | Internal firewall network |
| ATTACK_NET | em2 | ATTACK_NET | 10.10.20.1/24 | Isolated attacker network |

### KALI01

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Hostname | KALI01 |
| Interface | eth0 |
| IP Address | 10.10.20.10/24 |
| Default Gateway | 10.10.20.1 |
| Network | ATTACK_NET |

